<%# Chrome-free layout for printable pages (training sign-up sheet, trainer's
    report). No navbar, sidebar, or modal frame -- the browser's print output
    is the page itself; on-screen-only helpers inside the views use
    print:hidden. %>
<!DOCTYPE html>
<%# data-theme pins the light theme. This layout carries no navbar, so the
    theme controller never connects and <html> would otherwise stay bare --
    and daisyUI emits its dark theme under
    @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { :root:not([data-theme]) }. On a dark
    OS that flipped base-100 to near-black while the three hardcoded bridge
    tokens -- heading, body-subtle and line, which answer only to .dark or
    [data-theme="dark"] -- stayed light: a heading at 1.38:1 on the surface,
    measured. Body text was fine, because base-content is daisyUI's and moved
    with it. Pinning light makes the preview and the paper agree, and matches
    the sheet stylesheets, which fix their own ink on white in both themes. %>
<html lang="en" data-theme="light">
<head>
  <title><%= content_for(:title) || "Ranger Secret Clubhouse" %></title>
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
  <%= csrf_meta_tags %>
  <%= csp_meta_tag %>
  <%# The proportional roman latin face is on the critical path for every page. The
      italic, latin-ext and monospaced faces are declared in fonts.css and fetched
      only when something actually asks for them. %>
  <link rel="preload" href="<%= asset_path("atkinson-latin.woff2") %>" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
  <%= stylesheet_link_tag "tailwind", "data-turbo-track": "reload" %>
  <%# Letter with fixed margins for every print view. Lives here, not in the
      tailwind bundle -- @page cannot be scoped by selector, so a bare rule
      there would apply to every screen page's print output. %>
  <%# The :root rule covers the html box below the last sheet's content --
      daisyUI paints :root with base-100, and the body's print:bg-white
      cannot reach it. %>
  <style>
    @page { size: letter; margin: 0.5in; }
    @media print { :root { background: #fff; } }
  </style>
  <%# Named per-view @page rules land here via content_for :page_rules (the
      trainer's report emits its footer margin boxes with the dynamic session
      title; Chrome renders them -- verified in 151). CRITICAL: margin boxes
      must stay on a NAMED rule, never on the bare @page above -- that one
      reaches every print view, including the sign-up sheet, which carries no
      page numbers on purpose. %>
  <%= yield :page_rules %>
  <%= javascript_importmap_tags %>
  <%# Stimulus's own entry modules. They are inside the lazily-pinned controllers
      directory, so without these two the browser only discovers them after
      application.js has been fetched and parsed. %>
  <link rel="modulepreload" href="<%= asset_path("controllers/index.js") %>">
  <link rel="modulepreload" href="<%= asset_path("controllers/application.js") %>">
</head>
<%# print:bg-white -- paper is white regardless of the screen theme; the
    themed bg-base-100 tinted the trailing area of a report's final sheet. %>
<body class="bg-base-100 text-base-content text-base p-4 print:p-0 print:bg-white" data-controller="local-time">
<%= yield %>
</body>
</html>
